 "group_definition": "The leakage unit; a group is never split across locked/folds. * CRC647_<n>, jet-GC fuels: one group per fuel_id. * NIST_RP1 + its 3 RP-1 surrogates (Binary_2comp, Edwards_3comp, NIST_14comp): ONE group \"RP1\" - the surrogates are models of the same physical fuel and share its property targets. * gasoline: group = ``base_fuel``. FACE ethanol blends share their base gasoline (FACE_A x4 ...); the 66 bRON blends are a blendstock added to ONE of two base-gasoline lumps (63 / 3 blends), so per-blend random splitting would leak the base (R17: base RON/MON is a model input). Grouping by base keeps a base family on one side. Cost: the 63-blend bRON family is a single fold-sized group and bRON contributes no locked group.",
